; config options
server:
	target-fetch-policy: "0 0 0 0 0"
	qname-minimisation: no
	module-config: "validator cluster iterator"

cluster:
	cluster-peer: 10.0.0.1
	cluster-peer: 10.0.0.2
	cluster-peer: 10.0.0.3
	cluster-peer: 10.0.0.4
	cluster-self: 10.0.0.1
	cluster-timeout: 100

stub-zone:
	name: "example.com"
	stub-addr: 192.0.2.1
CONFIG_END

SCENARIO_BEGIN Cluster: the owner fails resolve requests that a fast local fallback resolves, it is resolve-ejected, probed hits still work, one trial request after the ejection time.
; 4 peers (10.0.0.1 is this node), at most floor(30% of 4) = 1 peer can be
; resolve-ejected.  The names are owned by 10.0.0.3, that answers the cache
; probes (MISS) but answers SERVFAIL to the resolve request (step 2) every
; time.  The local fallback resolves quickly (the authority answers at once),
; so the failure is charged to the owner.  Three charged failures in a row
; eject it: for a cache miss the owner is not asked to resolve (no step 2
; query), the miss is resolved locally.  A cache hit of the probe is still
; used.  After the ejection time (10 s, 20 s after a failed trial) exactly one
; trial resolve request is allowed; success ends the ejection.
; Answers of the owner have addresses 10.9.9.x, of the authority 10.8.8.x.
RANGE_BEGIN 0 100000
	ADDRESS 192.0.2.1
ENTRY_BEGIN
MATCH opcode qtype qname
ADJUST copy_id
REPLY QR AA NOERROR
SECTION QUESTION
q1.example.com. IN A
SECTION ANSWER
q1.example.com. 3600 IN A 10.8.8.1
ENTRY_END
ENTRY_BEGIN
